Let $A_0 =  F_0 -  \mathrm{cl}_N(F_0\cap A)$ and let $\T =  (T_1, \dots ,T_k)$ be an $F_0$-target and let $Y_0 = [A_0].$ 
We shall assume that $K= (P_1, \dots ,P_t)$ is a simple path-chain consistent with $\T$ rooted at $Y_0$ where for $\beta:[t] \rightarrow [k]$ we have $\forall i\in [t],\ y_{\beta(i)} \xrightarrow [W] {P_i} y_{\beta(i)}'.$  For all $i\in [t],$ let $a_{\beta(i)}' = \psi(y_{\beta(i)}').$  Our first task is to find conditions for $K$ such that when we exchange the elements $a_{\beta(i)}, i \in [t],$ in $A$ for the elements $a_{\beta(i)}',i \in [t]$, we achieve a new basis.

Recall that by the definition of an $F_0$-target, we have that $\forall a_i \in A^\spadesuit, \ T_i = C_i^*$ and $\forall a_i \in A - A^\spadesuit,\ T_i = F_i' = F_i \cap C_i^*.$ 

