49029:[McGuinness, *Rota's Basis Conjecture for Matroids with Density Close to One*](https://arxiv.org/abs/2107.07024) defines a rainbow basis by choosing one element from each coloured matroid basis, with the chosen elements themselves forming a basis. Two rainbow bases are disjoint when a colour never reuses an element. This generator gives the solver the uniform matroid `U_{n,n+2}` and `n` coloured bases, each encoded by the two ground elements it omits, and asks for the `n-2^3 = n-8` disjoint rainbow bases promised by Theorem 1.2.
