Implemented the Track B generator for [arXiv:2107.07024](https://arxiv.org/abs/2107.07024).

Deliverables:

- [gen_2107_07024.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.07024/gen_2107_07024.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.07024/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.07024/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.07024/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.07024/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.07024/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The inverse-generated family asks for \(n-8\) disjoint rainbow bases of \(U_{n,n+2}\). All local gates pass, including 0/200,000 random hits, four adversaries at 0/8, reference algorithm 8/8, and G9(c) at 209 atoms and 285 operations.

External hardening remains incomplete: easy was solved 3/3, medium 2/3, and the first hard attempt failed, after which OpenRouter returned total-key-limit errors. No hardened verdict was fabricated; the result should not be submitted until the bare and G9 runs complete after quota restoration.
